{
  "pages": [
    {
      "page_idx": 39,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.086,
            0.793,
            0.185
          ],
          "content": "Column 2: 4 × (r – 1) + 2 Column 3: 4 × (r – 1) + 3 Column 4: 4 × (r – 1) + 4 If c is the column number, then the general formula to generate all numbers is= 4 × (r – 1) + c"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.197,
            0.783,
            0.252
          ],
          "content": "**(b) In which row and column will the following numbers appear: (i) 124 (ii) 147 (iii) 201**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.267,
            0.721,
            0.287
          ],
          "content": "(i) We divide each number by 4 to find its row and column"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.186,
            0.301,
            0.615,
            0.398
          ],
          "content": "124 ÷ 4 So, Quotient = 31 and remainder is 0 ∴ 124 = 4 × 31 + 0 or 4 × 30 + 4 Comparing it with 4 × (r – 1) + c, we get r – 1 = 30, c = 4 So, r = 31 and c = 4"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.413,
            0.583,
            0.455
          ],
          "content": "(ii) 147 will appear at row 37 and column 3 (iii) 201 will appear at row 51 and column 1."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.481,
            0.752,
            0.536
          ],
          "content": "**(c) What number appears in row r and column c?** The number that appears in row r and column c is 4(r – 1) + c."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.561,
            0.554,
            0.581
          ],
          "content": "**(d) Observe the positions of multiples of 3.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.595,
            0.882,
            0.637
          ],
          "content": "The pattern in the columns in which multiples of 3 appear, follow a repeating sequence of column number: 3, 2, 1, 4, 3, 2, 1, ... as shown."
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "bbox": [
            0.359,
            0.664,
            0.638,
            0.901
          ],
          "content": "<table><tr><td colspan=4>1        2       3       4</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>2</td><td>3</td><td>4</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>6</td><td>7</td><td>8</td></tr><tr><td>9</td><td>10</td><td>11</td><td>12</td></tr><tr><td>13</td><td>14</td><td>15</td><td>16</td></tr><tr><td>--</td><td>-          --</td><td>----</td><td>---</td></tr></table>",
